# {{lb|en|of a process or thing}} Completed or done with [[efficiency]] and [[speed]]; [[facilitate|facilitating]] speed.
#* {{RQ:Scott Antiquary|I|VII|153|As they thus pressed forward, longing doubtless to exchange the easy curving line, which the sinuosities of the bay compelled them to adopt, for a straiter and more '''expeditious''' path, though less conformable to the line of beauty, Sir Arthur observed a human figure on the beach advancing to meet them.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Barry Lyndon|I return to Ireland, and exhibit my splendour and generosity in that kingdom|199|Now, there was a sort of rough-and-ready law in Ireland in those days which was of great convenience to persons desirous of '''expeditious''' justice{{nb...}}.}}

